    "`vips getpoint` on a .hdr prints FOUR values; the fourth is an out-of-bounds read (getpoint.c:105 sizes the array from the coded band count while vips_image_decode has already reduced the buffer to 3 bands). Every getpoint record here goes through rad2float first.",
    "Two different files named sample.hdr exist on this machine: 141x980 in the libviprs reference-test checkout and 1655x1764 in the libvips source tree. Records name which one they used.",
    "The existing oracle-captures/foreign/oracle.json record for loads['sample.hdr'] has the four-value getpoint bug baked in."
  ],
